<p><strong>To start a spa business in Nepal, define your services and customers, secure a location and the required registrations, hire and train therapists, and set up booking, payments and reporting from day one. Checking registration and licence rules with the relevant Nepali authorities comes first; this guide covers the operations side.</strong></p>
<p>This is an operations guide, not legal or tax advice. Rules for registration, licensing, health and tax can change, so confirm them with the relevant authorities and your accountant before you open.</p>
<h2>1. Decide what you sell and to whom</h2>
<p>Residents, office workers, tourists and couples want different things. Write down your service menu, durations and prices. A smaller menu done well beats a long one done unevenly.</p>
<h2>2. Plan rooms and therapists together</h2>
<p>A spa runs on two resources: the therapist and the room. A booking needs both. Plan how many rooms you have, how many therapists per shift and what happens between sessions. See <a href="/blog/how-to-manage-a-spa-in-nepal/">how to manage a spa in Nepal</a>.</p>
<h2>3. Take bookings in one place from day one</h2>
<p>Do not start with a notebook and plan to switch later. Start with an <a href="/solutions/spa/">online booking system built for spas</a> so guests book themselves and nothing is double-booked.</p>
<h2>4. Set discount and payment rules before you open</h2>
<ul>
<li>Who can give a discount, and who approves it? See <a href="/blog/discount-leakage/">discount leakage</a>.</li>
<li>How will you record cash, card and online payments? See <a href="/blog/daily-reconciliation/">daily reconciliation</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>5. Decide how you will reward regulars</h2>
<p>Memberships, packages and gift vouchers bring cash in early and bring customers back. Set them up carefully. See <a href="/blog/spa-memberships-packages-vouchers-nepal/">how to track them properly</a>.</p>
<h2>6. Pay your team fairly and clearly</h2>
<p>Agree salary, commission and attendance rules in writing. Tools like <a href="/features/payroll/">payroll</a> make month-end predictable.</p>
<h2>7. Plan for the second branch</h2>
<p>Choose tools that scale. Read the <a href="/blog/manage-multiple-spa-salon-branches-nepal/">multi-branch checklist</a> before you need it.</p>
